<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110397" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φᾱσιᾱνός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from the river Phasis</i>
			(v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φᾶσις</span>):—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ φ.</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρνις</span>), <i>the Phasian bird, pheasant, Phasianus
				colchicus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Mnesim.
				9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				109
			</span></i> (where some took it for <i>a Phasian horse,</i> cf. Sch.ad
			loc., <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				9.387a
			</span></i>, and cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φασιανοὶ ἵπποι,
				Φασιανικοὶ δὲ ὄρνεις</span> Hdn.Gr.post <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				p.459
			</span></i> Lobeck), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				557a12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				633b2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				180
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.Euerg.
				2
			</span></i>(b) <i><span class="en">J.,
					<u>Edict.Diocl.</u>4.17</span></i>
				(<u>Aeg.</u>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φ. ὄρνιθες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Callix.
					2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				14.654c
			</span></i>, etc.:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φασιανικός</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				68
			</span></i> (with a play on <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συκοφαντικός,</span> as <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φασιανὸς</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνήρ</span> represents <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συκοφάντης</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				726
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				1.83
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φ. ὄρνιθες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					6.52
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φ. στέαρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aët.
					5.118
				</span></i>
			.</div>
